      "content": "Example: try...catch...finally with Error"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Consider this code:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "content": "1try {\n2    console.log(result);\n3\n4} catch (error) {\n5    console.log(`Error caught: ${error}`);\n6\n7} finally {\n8\n9    // Code that runs regardless of error\n10    console.log(\"Finally executed\");\n11}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "Error caught: ReferenceError: result is not defined\nFinally executed"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In this example, the finally block executes after the exception is caught in the catch block."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Idea Emoji",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Now, let's see how finally behaves when no exception occurs."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
